      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STORMFRONT (4) gets the nod off a narrow BM76 second at this track, where he was well-supported favourite and beaten only a neck by Lim's Bighorn over 1600m. He is proven at this track and distance, carries 54kg, and the easier company makes him a big threat. HENNESSY LAD (6) is the major danger after putting a BM76 field away by just over six lengths at this venue, beating Fury and also holding a prior local edge over STORMFRONT. The return to 1300m is the main question, but his current form is strong. STRUCK GOLD (2) comes off a clean 1100m win in BM76 grade and has the 1300m record to remain a genuine hope. FIELD OF FLUTES (1) has won his past two, including a BM76 under 62.5kg, and his proven track-and-trip record keeps him firmly in the exotics mix despite the big weight and quick back-up.",
